WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:19.738
"What?" sheriff's cook was stunned by Little John's invitation.

2
00:00:19.758 --> 00:00:23.480
"You're asking me to join Robin Hood's band?

3
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.881
Are you one of his men?"

4
00:00:26.962 --> 00:00:28.082
Little John nodded.

5
00:00:28.102 --> 00:00:31.044
"My real name is Little John."

6
00:00:32.388 --> 00:00:33.189
"Little John!"

7
00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:34.470
exclaimed the cook.

8
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.972
"I've heard so much about you!

9
00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:38.994
But I never thought I'd meet you.

10
00:00:39.515 --> 00:00:42.137
And you live right here at the sheriff's house!"

11
00:00:43.598 --> 00:00:45.620
"That's right," said Little John.

12
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.563
"But it's time for me to return to my home in Sherwood Forest.

13
00:00:50.124 --> 00:00:52.786
Will you join me—and Robin Hood's band of men?"

14
00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:54.788
"Of course!"

15
00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:59.152
The cook was still staring at Little John in amazement.

16
00:00:59.896 --> 00:01:02.878
"I'd be glad to join Robin's band."

17
00:01:03.598 --> 00:01:04.759
Little John grinned.

18
00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:09.802
"Good. Let's take some of the sheriff's silver dishes," he said.

19
00:01:09.822 --> 00:01:12.683
"They'll make a fine gift for Robin."

20
00:01:12.703 --> 00:01:16.686
"Oh, yes," agreed the cook.

21
00:01:17.326 --> 00:01:19.888
"The sheriff has more silver than he can use."

22
00:01:21.088 --> 00:01:27.112
The two men looked around the room for silver, filling a sack with silver bowls, plates, and cups.

23
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.282
Then they set off for Sherwood Forest.

24
00:01:34.005 --> 00:01:36.828
At last they came to a large oak tree.

25
00:01:37.669 --> 00:01:41.172
Robin and a large group of men were lying in the shade on the grass.

26
00:01:41.192 --> 00:01:43.554
"It's Little John!"

27
00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:44.474
cried one.

28
00:01:45.155 --> 00:01:46.937
All the men jumped to their feet.

29
00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:49.439
"Welcome back, Little John!"

30
00:01:49.779 --> 00:01:50.460
said Robin.

31
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.442
"It's been a long time since we've seen you.

32
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:55.384
How was life with the sheriff?

33
00:01:55.988 --> 00:01:57.970
We heard you were one of his servants."

34
00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:04.394
"The sheriff treated me very well," replied Little John.

35
00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:08.497
"But I knew my real home was here in Sherwood Forest."

36
00:02:10.018 --> 00:02:10.899
The men cheered.

37
00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:13.581
"Hooray for Little John!"

38
00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:18.244
"I've brought my new friend, the sheriff's cook," said Little John.

39
00:02:18.264 --> 00:02:23.288
"And we've brought a gift—some of the sheriff's silver."

40
00:02:24.392 --> 00:02:27.855
Little John opened the sack and dumped the dishes on the ground.

41
00:02:28.595 --> 00:02:31.898
Everyone roared with laughter except Robin Hood.

42
00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.721
"I'm glad you're back," said Robin with a frown.

43
00:02:35.741 --> 00:02:38.683
"And I'm very happy that you brought a cook.

44
00:02:39.323 --> 00:02:41.945
But I don't like that you stole the sheriff's silver.

45
00:02:43.967 --> 00:02:47.669
He tried to fool me once and lost three hundred pounds.

46
00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.612
But he hasn't done anything wrong now."

47
00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.141
Little John shrugged.

48
00:02:54.161 --> 00:02:57.382
"Perhaps he'll be glad we have it," he said.

49
00:02:57.402 --> 00:03:00.823
"I have a thought—I'll go fetch him."

50
00:03:01.644 --> 00:03:06.105
With that, Little John dashed off through the forest to find the sheriff.

51
00:03:07.446 --> 00:03:09.727
The sheriff was still hunting with his friends.

52
00:03:11.368 --> 00:03:15.829
When Little John finally spotted him, he kneeled and removed his cap.

53
00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:17.870
"Greetings, master."

54
00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:20.771
"Reynold Greenleaf!"

55
00:03:21.152 --> 00:03:21.912
cried the sheriff.

56
00:03:22.632 --> 00:03:24.214
"What are you doing here in the woods?"

57
00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:29.118
"I've just seen the most amazing sight near an oak tree, master!"

58
00:03:29.598 --> 00:03:30.519
Little John said.

59
00:03:30.539 --> 00:03:36.424
"A huge green deer surrounded by many other green deer!"

60
00:03:37.565 --> 00:03:39.147
The sheriff stared at him.

61
00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.369
"That's quite a tale.

62
00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:42.790
Were you dreaming?"

63
00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.874
"No, I was wide awake," said Little John.

64
00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:49.376
"Come with me and see for yourself."

65
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.942
The sheriff was unsure of this tale, but he was also curious.

66
00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:59.125
So he let Little John lead him away from his friends.

67
00:03:59.725 --> 00:04:02.847
At last they drew close to the large oak tree.

68
00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:07.769
"I saw the herd somewhere around here," said Little John.

69
00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.732
The sheriff looked around—and spotted Robin and his men!

70
00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:16.854
He spun back toward Little John.

71
00:04:16.874 --> 00:04:18.735
"Now I know who you are.

72
00:04:18.975 --> 00:04:19.916
You're Little John!

73
00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.001
One day you'll pay for tricking me!"

74
00:04:23.741 --> 00:04:25.841
Robin came over and greeted the sheriff.

75
00:04:25.861 --> 00:04:27.502
"Welcome, Sheriff.

76
00:04:27.862 --> 00:04:29.663
Are you here for another feast?"

77
00:04:29.683 --> 00:04:32.903
"Oh no!"

78
00:04:33.424 --> 00:04:34.144
said the sheriff.

79
00:04:34.784 --> 00:04:39.325
He remembered the three hundred pounds he'd lost at Robin's last feast.

80
00:04:40.526 --> 00:04:43.887
"I'm not at all interested in feasting with you again!"

81
00:04:44.947 --> 00:04:45.767
Robin shrugged.

82
00:04:46.547 --> 00:04:48.268
"There's your cook," he said.

83
00:04:49.044 --> 00:04:51.025
"You can have anything you like to eat."

84
00:04:51.926 --> 00:04:53.827
The sheriff glared at his cook.

85
00:04:53.847 --> 00:04:56.008
"I'm not hungry."

86
00:04:57.869 --> 00:04:59.410
"Surely you'll have something to drink?"

87
00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:00.410
said Robin.

88
00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:04.933
One of Robin's men handed the sheriff a drink.

89
00:05:05.653 --> 00:05:06.854
The sheriff gasped.

90
00:05:06.874 --> 00:05:09.195
"That's my cup!"

91
00:05:09.535 --> 00:05:10.195
he shouted.

92
00:05:10.215 --> 00:05:12.597
"Do you like our new silver?"

93
00:05:12.997 --> 00:05:13.657
asked Robin.

94
00:05:13.677 --> 00:05:16.879
"We received a sack of it today."

95
00:05:17.599 --> 00:05:18.780
He held up the bag.

96
00:05:19.648 --> 00:05:22.570
The sheriff was so angry, he couldn't speak.

97
00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.031
He just stared at the ground.

98
00:05:25.051 --> 00:05:28.633
"You tried to trick me before," said Robin.

99
00:05:28.653 --> 00:05:31.334
"Instead I tricked you.

100
00:05:32.615 --> 00:05:35.156
But this time you weren't doing any harm.

101
00:05:35.917 --> 00:05:38.538
So leave the forest and take your silver with you."

102
00:05:39.359 --> 00:05:40.979
Robin handed him the bag.

103
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.761
The sheriff slowly reached for it.

104
00:05:45.362 --> 00:05:48.944
When he met his hunting friends later, they were full of questions.

105
00:05:51.312 --> 00:05:52.213
"Where did you go?"

106
00:05:52.233 --> 00:05:54.155
"What's in the bag?"

107
00:05:54.175 --> 00:05:56.197
"Where's Reynold Greenleaf?"

108
00:05:57.138 --> 00:06:01.922
The sheriff still felt dazed, confused thoughts tumbling inside his head.

109
00:06:01.942 --> 00:06:03.383
"Never mind.

110
00:06:03.543 --> 00:06:05.625
Forget about Reynold Greenleaf!"

111
00:06:05.966 --> 00:06:06.666
said the sheriff.

112
00:06:06.686 --> 00:06:08.208
"Let's go home."
